==============================================================================
G. Regular tournaments and the mean score (m-1)/2 (m <= 7)
==============================================================================
  m=3: mean score  1.0 = e(K_m)/m = Erdos--Sos density (t-2)/2 for t = m+1 = 4:  whole (regular tournaments exist)
  m=4: mean score  1.5 = e(K_m)/m = Erdos--Sos density (t-2)/2 for t = m+1 = 5:  half (no regular tournament; near-regular only)
  m=5: mean score  2.0 = e(K_m)/m = Erdos--Sos density (t-2)/2 for t = m+1 = 6:  whole (regular tournaments exist)
  m=6: mean score  2.5 = e(K_m)/m = Erdos--Sos density (t-2)/2 for t = m+1 = 7:  half (no regular tournament; near-regular only)
  m=7: mean score  3.0 = e(K_m)/m = Erdos--Sos density (t-2)/2 for t = m+1 = 8:  whole (regular tournaments exist)
  The unique near-regular tournament on 4 vertices is S4 (scores 1,1,2,2); the unique
  acyclic one is TT4; the converse pair A/B sits between them.

