==============================================================================
I. Collatz inverse step integrality: period-2 rhythm from ord_3(2) = 2 (m odd, m <= 10^5)
==============================================================================
  n = (2^k m - 1)/3 is whole iff 2^k m = 1 (mod 3): k even for m = 1 (mod 3), k odd for m = 2 (mod 3),
  never for 3 | m.  Period 2 = ord_3(2).  The Erdos--Sos alternation is 2 | 3n, i.e. 2 | n: period 2
  from the prime 2 itself.  Same period, different mechanism (multiplicative order vs divisibility).

