==============================================================================
J. The Klein-group dictionary: end-folds of P_5 vs boundary arc flips of TT_4
==============================================================================
  P5 after id: path P_5               diameter 4  (u = 4 - diameter = 0)
  P5 after L : spider/fork deg=[3, 2, 1, 1, 1] diameter 3  (u = 4 - diameter = 1)
  P5 after R : spider/fork deg=[3, 2, 1, 1, 1] diameter 3  (u = 4 - diameter = 1)
  P5 after LR: star K_{1,4}           diameter 2  (u = 4 - diameter = 2)
  TT4 after id: scores (0, 1, 2, 3)  TT4 (u=0)
  TT4 after L : scores (0, 2, 2, 2)  3-cycle over sink (u=1)
  TT4 after R : scores (1, 1, 1, 3)  source over 3-cycle (u=1)
  TT4 after LR: scores (1, 1, 2, 2)  strong S4 (u=2)
  rho(i) = 5-i is an automorphism of the path but an anti-automorphism of TT4: it identifies
  fork_L with fork_R, and identifies the two diamonds only after converse-merging.  Merged label
  u = #boundary defects (THM-584) <-> 4 - diameter;  H = 2u+1 = 1,3,5;  leaves = u+2 = 2,3,4.

==============================================================================
K. Fork-free structure lemma and exact ex(n, fork) = ex(n, P5) = 6 floor(n/4) + C(n mod 4, 2)
==============================================================================
  structure lemma agrees with direct subgraph search on all 1252 atlas graphs (<= 7 vertices)
  and on 3000 random graphs with 8..12 vertices
  Proof: a vertex c of degree >= 3 whose neighbour a has a neighbour outside N[c] gives a fork; so N[c] is a
  component; if deg c >= 4 any edge inside N(c) gives a fork, so the component is a star; if deg c = 3 the
  component has 4 vertices.  Hence fork-free components are stars, paths, cycles or <= 4 vertices, and the
  maximum edge count is 6 floor(n/4) + C(r,2): disjoint K4's plus a clique on the remainder (Erdos--Gallai/
  Faudree--Schelp give the same value for P5).

  n   3n/2   ex(star)  ex(path)=ex(fork)   deficit star   deficit path/fork
   4    6.0       6            6             0.0            0.0
   5    7.5       7            6             0.5            1.5
   6    9.0       9            7             0.0            2.0
   7   10.5      10            9             0.5            1.5
   8   12.0      12           12             0.0            0.0
   9   13.5      13           12             0.5            1.5
  10   15.0      15           13             0.0            2.0
  11   16.5      16           15             0.5            1.5
  12   18.0      18           18             0.0            0.0
  13   19.5      19           18             0.5            1.5
  14   21.0      21           19             0.0            2.0
  15   22.5      22           21             0.5            1.5
  16   24.0      24           24             0.0            0.0
  deficit(star) has period 2 (handshake parity); deficit(path/fork) has period 4 (K4 packing residue).

